#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:15
msgid "Install Python Interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:17
msgid ""
":ref:`piocore` is written in `Python <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_ "
"that is installed by default on all the popular OSs except Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:20
msgid ""
"Please navigate to official website and `Download the latest Python <https://"
"www.python.org/downloads/>`_ and install it. Please **READ NOTES BELOW**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:0
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:24
msgid ""
"Most linux distributions will include a Python installation already. You may "
"need to ensure that the Python Virtual Environment is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:26
msgid "Debian/Ubuntu derivatives have this package in Apt as ``python3-venv``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:28
msgid "``sudo apt install python3-venv`` should be all that is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:30
msgid ""
"For more details, please check the `platformio-core-installer/issues/85 "
"<https://github.com/platformio/platformio-core-installer/issues/85>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:0
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:33
msgid ""
"Please read the \"Important Information\" displayed during installation for "
"information about SSL/TLS certificate validation and the running the "
"**\"Install Certificates.command\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:36
msgid ""
"If you do not install SSL/TLS certificates, PlatformIO will not be able to "
"download dependent packages, libraries, and toolchains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:0
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../faq/install-python.rst:40
msgid ""
"Please select ``Add Python to Path`` (see below), otherwise, ``python`` "
"command will not be available."
msgstr ""
